[{"answer":"I went to England with my mother.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/1.mp3"},{"answer":"She used to be a singer in a band.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/2.mp3"},{"answer":"We went to the hotel that she used to sing at.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/3.mp3"},{"answer":"It was a big fancy hotel.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/4.mp3"},{"answer":"Some of the people that she knew when she sang in the band were still there.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/5.mp3"},{"answer":"They remembered my mother, and they had a good time talking to her and remembering old times.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/6.mp3"},{"answer":"Many people told me that I looked like my mother.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/7.mp3"},{"answer":"In the hotel, they had a fancy hall where they had ballroom dancing.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/8.mp3"},{"answer":"I am not used to that kind of dancing.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/9.mp3"},{"answer":"I always dance to rock music.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/10.mp3"},{"answer":"A man told me that he would teach me how to dance.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/11.mp3"},{"answer":"It looked very easy.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/12.mp3"},{"answer":"I held one of his hands, and put my other hand on his shoulder.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/13.mp3"},{"answer":"He told me exactly how to move my feet.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/14.mp3"},{"answer":"I was very clumsy, and I stepped on his toes.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/15.mp3"},{"answer":"He was patient with me, and he counted \"one, two, three\".","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/16.mp3"},{"answer":"I tried to waltz with him.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/17.mp3"},{"answer":"I would start out pretty well, but then I would get mixed up and stand on his toes again.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/18.mp3"},{"answer":"The man laughed about it.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/19.mp3"},{"answer":"I told him that I wasn't a very good dancer, but he said that I was good for a beginner.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/20.mp3"},{"answer":"I think he was just being polite.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/21.mp3"},{"answer":"The man asked my mother to dance.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/22.mp3"},{"answer":"My mother is a very good dancer.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/23.mp3"},{"answer":"I didn't know that about her.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/24.mp3"},{"answer":"She never stepped on the man's toes once.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/25.mp3"},{"answer":"The man thanked us for dancing with him, and I thanked him for giving me dancing lessons.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/26.mp3"},{"answer":"I don't think I'll ever be very good at that type of dancing.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/27.mp3"},{"answer":"Each generation has a specific type of dancing.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/28.mp3"},{"answer":"The way that I dance is different from the way that my mother dances.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/29.mp3"},{"answer":"The way that I dance doesn't involve moving your feet too much.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/30.mp3"},{"answer":"I'm not too good at fancy steps.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/general-english/112-learning-to-dance-2019-04-07-03-58-55/31.mp3"}]
